# Persist saved Analysis items

Prevent saved production checks and plans from disappearing when Analysis is dismissed and reopened.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Saving a production check or plan writes it to persistent application/game state rather than sheet-local view state.
- [ ] Saved items remain available after closing and reopening Analysis.
- [ ] Saved items remain associated with their player, kind, icon, name, cards, and ordered construction steps.
- [ ] Editing an existing item updates the persisted item without creating a duplicate.
- [ ] Existing saved-data decoding remains backward compatible, including records without a selected icon.
- [ ] Persistence ownership avoids global mutable state and preserves serializability.
- [ ] Domain regression coverage verifies save, reload, edit, player isolation, and kind isolation.
- [ ] App, unit-test, and UI-test bundles compile.
- [ ] Focused persistence checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Scope notes

- This is the critical REQ-017 defect and should be completed before the remaining REQ-017 presentation tasks.
- Do not implement simulation storage or a broader game-document system unless separately required.
